  "intentional_diffs": [
    "1. repo identity (AC3): `materialize_child_issues._require_trusted_repo` (repo_identity.py loaded from its fixed on-disk path, fail-closed) runs in `materialize()` before any runner call and in `apply_parent_checklist_patch()` before any gh call; the CLI exits 2 (PLAN_VALIDATION_ERROR: repo_untrusted). Source only forwarded `--repo` to gh.",
    "2. tests/create-issue/conftest.py is the SOURCE conftest (child-plan fixtures restored; the Stage 2-5 shim deferred them to #36) with the legacy plan repo replaced by `TRUSTED_REPO` read from repo_identity.py.",
    "3. Legacy slug / placeholder repos in the migrated tests (`o/r`, the legacy slug) are replaced by `TRUSTED_REPO` (repo_identity.py) so no functional slug constant is added; the no-functional-slug check stays green.",
    "4. The two fake-gh integration tests in test_materialize_child_issues_no_raw_gh.py now use the Stage 2-5 stateful fake gh (tests/stage2/fixtures/fake_gh_create.py). The source's hand-written fake predated the txn's body readback and the approved-operation gate. Positive path: empty --issue-kind (kind from the body MRC, label-free), no parent, no dependency. The CLI path asserts the gate refuses the implementation-kind/parent create with zero `issue create`/`issue edit` calls.",
    "5. tests/create-issue/* are Ruff-clean (format, import order, `check=False`, removesuffix); `.claude/skills/**` stays excluded by pyproject (not changed).",
    "6. .claude/skills/create-issue/SKILL.md: the Stage 2-5 'unmigrated' note is replaced by the 2-6a status; the procedure text is unchanged.",
    "7. New: tests/stage2/test_stage2_6_materialization.py (AC1/AC3/AC4 closure and negative controls), this manifest, CI lane stage2-6-materialization.",
    "8. Hardening found by independent review (materialize_child_issues): (a) a txn result with rc 0 but status other than `success` (e.g. `dedupe`) is recorded in affected_issues + errors, never as created, and blocks the parent patch; (b) a non-numeric txn issue_number is an error, not an exception; (c) apply_parent_checklist_patch rejects old_line/new_line containing line breaks/control characters, refuses parent bodies with non-LF line breaks, splits on LF only (lossless join), and requires the read-back body to equal the patched body exactly (not only the Child Issues section)."
  ],
  "known_source_defects": [
    {
      "id": "parent-link-always-gated",
      "where": "materialize() -> _default_create_runner",
      "detail": "the materializer always passes the parent issue (and renders a Parent reference into the body) and the default `standard` label profile with an explicit implementation kind, so create_issue_txn's Stage 2-5 gate refuses every real child create (`unapproved-operation`: label / parent / dependency) before any gh call. The lane is therefore fail-closed end to end; a successful child create exists only for the label-free, parent-free shape.",
      "owner": "squne121/agent-platform#46 (native relationship approval) - not decided here"
    },
    {
      "id": "research-kind-render-fails-validation",
      "where": "render_canonical_body(kind=research)",
      "detail": "observed: a research child rendered by render_canonical_body fails validate_issue_body (LP017 Stop Conditions). Not fixed (source behaviour, no AC depends on it).",
      "owner": "unassigned"
    },
    {
      "id": "parent-patch-uses-direct-gh-edit",
      "where": "apply_parent_checklist_patch",
      "detail": "the `## Child Issues` checklist patch is a direct `gh issue edit --body-file` guarded by the parent body_sha256 precondition, exactly-one-match and a section-scoped readback; it does not go through edit_issue_txn (which needs a readiness forwarding payload). Gated here by the trusted-repo check and only reachable after a fully clean create.",
      "owner": "human decision (see human_judgment_required)"
    }
  ],
